{"id": "EUVD-2026-86730", "enisaUuid": "328db525-0060-30d3-92e8-cb9998e0d1dd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nieee802154: hwsim: serialize pib updates to fix double-free\n\nhwsim_update_pib() does an unserialized read-swap-free of phy->pib:\n\n\tpib_old = rtnl_dereference(phy->pib);\n\t...\n\trcu_assign_pointer(phy->pib, pib);\n\tkfree_rcu(pib_old, rcu);\n\nIt assumes the RTNL is held, but ->set_channel is not always called\nunder it: the mac802154 scan worker changes channels via\ndrv_set_channel() without the RTNL. Such an update can race an\nRTNL-held one on the same phy; both read the same pib_old and both\nkfree_rcu() it, double-freeing the object. With SLUB percpu sheaves\nbatching kfree_rcu(), this surfaces as a KASAN invalid-free in\nrcu_free_sheaf().\n\nstruct hwsim_phy has no lock for pib. Add one and make the swap atomic\nwith rcu_replace_pointer() under it, dropping the misleading\nrtnl_dereference().", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3b4681197aa026bd2d79358de5a3d62b76b04b9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9973b3a67a7592a780ea12b08334539a900deec1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3b8f264ce09573aededd0a97dc41c8147797d8f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db6442deecb1f13aeaf4f9d77746ea7555630fb3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/979d5b8de8ed4e1f997aef12da5694b99be7b871"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97599", "GHSA-r8g8-vw6g-m8xh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0aeba280-acdb-34f4-b1fa-d5ece7348ba5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f25da51fdc381ca2863248c7060b3662632f0872 <e3b4681197aa026bd2d79358de5a3d62b76b04b9"}, {"id": "20877717-e12c-352b-a624-6086a2180e0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "26fdc74b-f4fd-3aa6-89b6-e7865bb93a3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "494f9481-9267-302d-a0a1-af09082a231c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "566a7de3-c360-3c5a-9bb7-dc8438c2ff2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f25da51fdc381ca2863248c7060b3662632f0872 <979d5b8de8ed4e1f997aef12da5694b99be7b871"}, {"id": "626d731b-1f0e-3e44-923d-5e26b1679bc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "63c070da-7ab6-378a-8d04-e5300ac1e4d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f25da51fdc381ca2863248c7060b3662632f0872 <9973b3a67a7592a780ea12b08334539a900deec1"}, {"id": "9427589a-9cd6-3586-82c1-123c86364096", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "96d3e284-ac48-33b8-9e60-11bdc9e5be26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "97ae51a1-0566-31ce-8880-8da1ae670721", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f25da51fdc381ca2863248c7060b3662632f0872 <db6442deecb1f13aeaf4f9d77746ea7555630fb3"}, {"id": "9bb3ed91-29e5-3ed5-8c9a-05db01e18d0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f25da51fdc381ca2863248c7060b3662632f0872 <d3b8f264ce09573aededd0a97dc41c8147797d8f"}, {"id": "f9b0f11f-14a8-3d5d-a363-acf1faad1b4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dd8b2cd7-b3c4-305a-ac1e-7bb0fd13e870", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}